.TH NINIT-SHUTDOWN 8 2026-09-24 "ninit @PACKAGE_VERSION@"
.SH NAME
ninit-shutdown \- reboot, halt or power off a system running ninit
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B shutdown
.RI [ option ]...\&
.I time
.RI [ message ]
.br
.BR poweroff | reboot | halt
.RI [ option ]...\&
.RI [ time ]
.br
.B telinit
.BR 0 | 6 | q
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ninit\-shutdown
is installed under the names
.BR shutdown ,
.BR poweroff ,
.BR reboot ,
.B halt
and
.BR telinit .
the name it is invoked by selects the default action:
.B reboot
reboots,
.B halt
halts, and every other name powers off.
invoked as
.BR ninit\-shutdown ,
it behaves as
.B shutdown
.PP
it performs, in order:
.IP 1. 4
if
.I /proc/1/comm
can be read and is not
.BR ninit ,
execute
.IB name .old
from its own directory with the same arguments, where
.I name
is the name it was invoked by
.IP 2. 4
with
.BR \-f ,
call
.BR sync (2)
and
.BR reboot (2)
.IP 3. 4
if
.I time
is in the future, write a notice to
.I /dev/console
and wait in the foreground.
.B SIGINT
cancels
.IP 4. 4
if the effective user is root, send
.B SIGTERM
(reboot),
.B SIGUSR1
(halt) or
.B SIGUSR2
(power off) to process 1
.IP 5. 4
otherwise, call the
.BR Reboot ,
.B Halt
or
.B PowerOff
method of
.B org.freedesktop.login1.Manager
on the system bus through
.BR dbus\-send (1),
leaving the decision to elogind and polkit
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-r
reboot
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-P ", " \-p
power off
.TP
.B \-H
halt
.TP
.B \-f
sync and call
.BR reboot (2)
directly.
services are not stopped and filesystems are not remounted
.TP
.B \-c
refused.
a pending shutdown runs in the foreground and is cancelled by interrupting it
.TP
.BI \-t " sec" "\fR, \fP" \-k "\fR, \fP" \-n "\fR, \fP" \-w "\fR, \fP" \-d
accepted and ignored
.TP
.B \-\-help
print usage
.SH OPERANDS
.TP
.I time
.BR now ,
.BI + minutes ,
or
.IB hh : mm
in local time, meaning its next occurrence.
required by
.BR shutdown .
operands after
.IR time ,
such as a message, are ignored
.TP
.BR 0 | 6 | q
the runlevel operand of
.BR telinit .
.B 0
powers off,
.B 6
reboots and
.B q
does nothing
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
the request was delivered
.TP
.B 1
a request that could not be delivered, or a failure to execute
.IB name .old
.TP
.B 2
an invalid option or operand
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /proc/1/comm
identifies
.B ninit
as process 1
.TP
.IB name .old
the program this one replaced, installed by
.B make tools\-install
.SH NOTES
.B make tools\-install
renames each existing
.BR shutdown ,
.BR poweroff ,
.BR halt ,
.B reboot
and
.B telinit
in sbindir to
.IB name .old
and replaces it with a symbolic link to
.BR ninit\-shutdown .
an existing
.IB name .old
is never replaced.
.B make tools\-uninstall
restores the originals
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ninit (8),
.BR ninitctl (8),
.BR reboot (2)
